{"id": "d67a51c6-a02b-4bcc-ada8-33e1e76b514b", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll scan the customer-managed IAM policies and measure each policy document against the 6,144-character managed policy limit. IAM doesn't count whitespace toward that limit. Then I'll rank them by how close they are.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_lBAjdmZ8cTSG6umBSjHPCE", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "iam-policy-size-audit", "agent_type": "generic", "prompt": "{
  "task": "Audit all customer-managed IAM policies (Scope=Local) for size against the IAM managed policy size limit and rank them by how close they are to the limit.",
  "context": "User wants to know which customer-managed IAM policies are closest to the IAM managed policy size quota. IAM is a global service; use aws_region us-east-1. Start with the agent space's own account 012345678901_1, then use list_associations to find any other associated AWS accounts and audit those too (read-only operations only; report any account you can't access).",
  "approach_hints": "Use iam list_policies (Scope=Local, paginate fully, OnlyAttached=False), then for each policy call get_policy to find DefaultVersionId and get_policy_version to fetch the default version document. Compute the size as the number of characters in the policy document JSON EXCLUDING all whitespace (spaces, tabs, newlines), since IAM's 6,144-character managed policy limit does not count whitespace. Verify the current limit with verify_aws_claim if unsure (expected: 6,144 non-whitespace characters for managed policies). Compute sizes by actually counting characters, not estimating. If there are many policies, process them efficiently and keep only the summary in your final answer.",
  "criteria": "Return: total number of customer-managed policies per account; a ranked table of the top ~15 policies by size (account, policy name, size in non-whitespace characters, percent of 6,144 limit, attached entity count if easily available); flag any policies at or above ~80% of the limit; note the total count of policies above 50%. Also mention any policies you could not read. Keep the final report concise."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit customer-managed IAM policy sizes against limit"}], "created_at": null}

